---Represents a Google Tag Manager Tag.
---@class gcp.tagmanager_v2.Tag
---@field scheduleEndMs? string The end timestamp in milliseconds to schedule a tag.
---@field tagId? string The Tag ID uniquely identifies the GTM Tag.
---@field parameter? gcp.tagmanager_v2.ParameterList The tag's parameters.
---@field containerId? string GTM Container ID.
---@field monitoringMetadata? gcp.tagmanager_v2.Parameter A map of key-value pairs of tag metadata to be included in the event data for tag monitoring. Notes: - This parameter must be type MAP. - Each parameter in the map are type TEMPLATE, however cannot contain variable references.
---@field setupTag? gcp.tagmanager_v2.SetupTagList The list of setup tags. Currently we only allow one.
---@field teardownTag? gcp.tagmanager_v2.TeardownTagList The list of teardown tags. Currently we only allow one.
---@field name? string Tag display name.
---@field accountId? string GTM Account ID.
---@field firingTriggerId? gcp.tagmanager_v2.StringList Firing trigger IDs. A tag will fire when any of the listed triggers are true and all of its blockingTriggerIds (if any specified) are false.
---@field tagManagerUrl? string Auto generated link to the tag manager UI
---@field fingerprint? string The fingerprint of the GTM Tag as computed at storage time. This value is recomputed whenever the tag is modified.
---@field path? string GTM Tag's API relative path.
---@field workspaceId? string GTM Workspace ID.
---@field monitoringMetadataTagNameKey? string If non-empty, then the tag display name will be included in the monitoring metadata map using the key specified.
---@field scheduleStartMs? string The start timestamp in milliseconds to schedule a tag.
---@field liveOnly? boolean If set to true, this tag will only fire in the live environment (e.g. not in preview or debug mode).
---@field parentFolderId? string Parent folder id.
---@field tagFiringOption? gcp.tagmanager_v2.TagTagFiringOptionEnum|string Option to fire this tag.
---@field paused? boolean Indicates whether the tag is paused, which prevents the tag from firing.
---@field consentSettings? gcp.tagmanager_v2.TagConsentSetting Consent settings of a tag.
---@field blockingTriggerId? gcp.tagmanager_v2.StringList Blocking trigger IDs. If any of the listed triggers evaluate to true, the tag will not fire.
---@field notes? string User notes on how to apply this tag in the container.
---@field priority? gcp.tagmanager_v2.Parameter User defined numeric priority of the tag. Tags are fired asynchronously in order of priority. Tags with higher numeric value fire first. A tag's priority can be a positive or negative value. The default value is 0.
---@field type? string GTM Tag Type.

---@class gcp.tagmanager_v2.TagConsentSetting
---@field consentStatus? gcp.tagmanager_v2.TagConsentSettingConsentStatusEnum|string The tag's consent status. If set to NEEDED, the runtime will check that the consent types specified by the consent_type field have been granted.
---@field consentType? gcp.tagmanager_v2.Parameter The type of consents to check for during tag firing if in the consent NEEDED state. This parameter must be of type LIST where each list item is of type STRING.

---@alias gcp.tagmanager_v2.TagConsentSettingConsentStatusEnum "notSet"|"notNeeded"|"needed"

---@alias gcp.tagmanager_v2.TagList gcp.tagmanager_v2.Tag[]

---@alias gcp.tagmanager_v2.TagTagFiringOptionEnum "tagFiringOptionUnspecified"|"unlimited"|"oncePerEvent"|"oncePerLoad"

